hild;\n./README.md-24-- clones only the chosen reference track's file-backed media to the mirror track, without adding sends, changing source tracks, or changing project tempo/sample rate;\n./README.md:25:- writes the adjacent `.vgt` sidecar — named after the project, e.g. `Reaper Project.vgt` — with schema version 1, its two created track GUIDs, and config recording the reference track;\n./README.md-26-- on re-apply, deletes only tracks whose GUID occurs in the sidecar **and** whose current name begins `[vgt]`, then recreates the same area.\n./README.md-27-\n./README.md-28-The folder/mirror are therefore idempotent and original tracks remain untouched. REAPER-native click-source items have no file to clone, so choosing a click track mirrors nothing. `vgt apply` validates the project path and directs you to this action rather than silently falling back to unsafe RPP editing.\n./README.md-29-\n./README.md-30-Automation can skip the menu by setting the `vgt`/`reference_index` ExtState (a 0-based index over the non-`[vgt]` tracks) before running the action; interactive users are always prompted.\n--\n./README.md-35-[Phase 0 live verification](docs/phase0-live-verification.md). The verifier\n./README.md-36-checks the saved RPP and sidecar after both the first apply and re-apply.\n./README.md-37-\n./README.md-38-## Analyze the reference track (Phase 1)\n./README.md-39-\n./README.md:40:`vgt analyze [project.rpp]` requires a `.vgt` sidecar already written by the\n./README.md-41-apply action above. It resolves the reference track's source audio file,\n./README.md-42-runs the tempo/key/sections/chords detectors, and writes the results back\n./README.md-43-into the sidecar as schema version 2 — never inside REAPER itself.\n./README.md-44-\n./README.md-45-Each detector's output is cached against a hash of the source audio and the\n--\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md-86-\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md-87-### Manifest sketch\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md-88-\n./docs/phase1-