me>`;\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md-56-- the sidecar GUIDs are exactly the two `[vgt]` tracks: the reference-named\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md-57-  folder with depth `+1`, followed by one `[vgt] Mirror` child with depth `-1`;\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md-58-- the mirror has exactly the chosen reference track's file-backed media items,\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md-59-  all of which resolve on disk. Thus the second pass also rejects duplicate\n--\n./docs/GOAL.md-23-functionality.\n./docs/GOAL.md-24-\n./docs/GOAL.md-25-## Phases\n./docs/GOAL.md-26-\n./docs/GOAL.md-27-The initiative is built in incremental phases. Each adds a self-contained slice and builds on the `[vgt]`\n./docs/GOAL.md:28:conventions and the `<project>.vgt` sidecar established by the phases before it. \"Done\" for the whole project is\n./docs/GOAL.md-29-the union of every phase's deliverables below.\n./docs/GOAL.md-30-\n./docs/GOAL.md-31-### Phase 0 — REAPER-plumbing foundation *(delivered)*\n./docs/GOAL.md-32-\n./docs/GOAL.md-33-Establishes how vgt locates, opens, and safely augments a REAPER project, and where vgt stores its own state.\n--\n./docs/GOAL.md-37-  working directory, assume the user wants to work with that one;\n./docs/GOAL.md-38-- **opening the project and reading relevant information** — parse the project and read at least: sample rate,\n./docs/GOAL.md-39-  tempo/time-signature, and the existing track list (names and GUIDs) so vgt can tell which tracks are already\n./docs/GOAL.md-40-  vgt-managed;\n./docs/GOAL.md-41-- **storing vgt settings next to the REAPER project** — a single sidecar file living alongside the\n./docs/GOAL.md:42:  `.RPP` and sharing its name with a `.vgt` extension (e.g. `Reaper Project.RPP` → `Reaper Project.vgt`), holding\n./docs/GOAL.md-43-  vgt's own state (schema version, the vgt-managed track GUIDs it created, and any config);\n./docs/GOAL.md-44-- **preparing a \"vgt managed\" area for practice tracks** — a REAPER track folder (and 